<title>Hereditary Spherocytosis: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0265-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Patient with DAT-negative hemolytic anemia, spherocytes, and increased MCHC</label>
<path target="cell-2"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Family history of hereditary spherocytosis?</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Typical clinical and laboratory features?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Diagnosis confirmed, no further workup necessary.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Typical clinical and laboratory features?</label>
<path target="cell-9">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Reconsider other diagnoses. Additional testing as indicated.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-9">
<label>Confirmed with flow cytometry (EMA) or cryohemolysis (alternatively osmotic fragility)?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-10">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-10">
<label>Confirmed with SDS-PAGE?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-8">No</path>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>DAT, direct antiglobulin test; EMA, flow cytometry using eosin-5- maleimide; SDS-PAGE, sodium dodecyl sulfate polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis.</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
